lesson: 230
title: Letters, colours and points
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: The English alphabet has 26 letters. Five of them, a, e, i, o and u, are vowels; in this lesson every other letter, y too, is a consonant.
explain: So the alphabet has 26 − 5 = 21 consonants. A rainbow has 7 colours, a clock face 12 numbers and a compass 4 main points.
explain: 3 children each write every consonant once: 3 × 21 = 63 consonants.
vars: a=name k=2..9
answer: k * 21
exercise: {k} children each write every consonant of the alphabet on a card, one letter per card. How many cards do they write?
exercise: {a} writes each consonant of the alphabet {k} times for handwriting practice. How many letters does {a.he} write?
exercise: A teacher cuts out every consonant of the alphabet for each of {k} groups. How many letters does she cut out?
exercise: {a} makes {k} sets of letter tiles, each set with all the consonants of the alphabet. How many tiles is that?
exercise: Each of {k} classes paints all the consonants of the alphabet on the playground wall. How many consonants are painted?
exercise: every consonant on a card, {k} sets. how many cards
exercise: {a} copies the consonants out {k+1} times — no, {k} times. how many letters
exercise: {k} of us each do all the consonants in glitter lol. how many letters
exercise: my bro reckons there's {k*20} consonants in {k} alphabets. how many really
exercise: {a} paints {k} rainbows and then writes all the consonants {k} times underneath. How many consonants does {a.he} write?
exercise: How many consonants are there in {k} copies of the alphabet?
test: For each of {k} pupils, the teacher prints the consonants of the alphabet on cards. How many cards does she print?
test: How many consonant tiles are in {k} full alphabet sets, if the vowel tiles are taken out?
test: all the letters but the vowels, {k} times, how many is that
test: {a} writes out the whole alphabet {k} times and then rubs out every vowel. How many letters are left?
test: {k} kids, each needs every consonant for the wall, and {k+2} rainbow posters too. how many consonant cards
test: Without the vowels, how many letters does {a} stamp if {a.he} stamps the alphabet {k} times?
exam: Determine the aggregate number of consonants contained in {k.words} complete copies of the English alphabet.
exam: It is given that each of {k} pupils inscribes every consonant of the English alphabet exactly once. Ascertain the total number of letters so inscribed.
exam: Whereas the vowels are excluded, state the number of letters remaining when the English alphabet is written out {k} times in full.
exam: Compute the number of cards required to display each consonant of the English alphabet once for every one of {k} groups.
exercise: The teacher says {a}'s handwriting "has room for improvement", so {a} writes out every consonant of the alphabet {k} times. How many consonants does {a} write?
exercise: teacher reckons i'm "a little chatty in class" so it's lines: every consonant {k} times. that's bloody loads. how many letters
test: {a}'s report said {a.he} "tries hard" at spelling, so Gran gives {a.him} practice: every consonant once on each of {k} pages. How many letters is that?
